;; Seed Genome topology (component).
;;
;; Executable chain (the M2 fixture's :llm planner is replaced by the
;; :sci router as the ENTRY — the v0 runtime registry implements no
;; :llm handler, so the entry must be an executable node):
;;
;;     :node/router (:sci, :program/route) → :node/tool → :node/emit
;;
;; The route program (programs/route.clj) is the seed's decision-maker:
;; for {:op :echo :text "abc"} it EMITS the typed :intent/tool-call for
;; :fixture/echo, which the component scheduler dispatches through the
;; kernel-owned broker — that is the session's ONE authorized tool call
;; and ONE provider result. The :tool node then exercises the :tool
;; handler path against :fixture/non-idempotent, a REGISTERED provider
;; OUTSIDE the host's granted lease, so the broker scope-denies it
;; (:intent/denied) — demonstrating Global Constraint 9 (a visible tool
;; never grants resource authority) inside the same run. The :emit node
;; completes the session with the accumulated outputs.
;;
;; The graph is acyclic (compile-topology rejects raw cycles; only
;; explicit :loop nodes may iterate), so it compiles with the step
;; budget :limits {:max-steps 64}.
{:graph/id :graph/seed
 :entry :node/router
 :nodes
 {:node/router {:node/type :sci
                :program :program/route
                :next :node/tool}
  :node/tool   {:node/type :tool
                :tool :fixture/non-idempotent
                :next :node/emit}
  :node/emit   {:node/type :emit}}
 :limits {:max-steps 64}}
